# 6. MOTION DESIGN SYSTEM

Motion is a central part of this product.

Build reusable animation components and establish consistent animation rules.

## Page Entrance

* Navigation enters smoothly from above.
* Headline reveals progressively.
* Supporting text fades upward.
* Buttons enter with staggered timing.
* Hero tree branches grow progressively.
* Decorative elements settle naturally.

## Scroll Animation

As users scroll:

* Content reveals with gentle fade and upward movement.
* Section headings reveal in sequence.
* Cards appear with staggered timing.
* Feature demonstrations animate into view.
* Tree connection illustrations draw progressively.

Use Intersection Observer or an equivalent efficient mechanism.

Do not trigger expensive animations continuously.

## Buttons

Buttons should have:

* Subtle hover lift.
* Smooth color transitions.
* Refined shadow transitions.
* Responsive pressed states.
* Clear loading states.

## Cards

Cards should have:

* Small hover elevation.
* Smooth transition.
* Optional subtle border highlight.
* No exaggerated movement.

## Tree Motion

Family tree interactions must feel exceptionally polished.

When expanding a branch:

* Connection lines extend.
* Child nodes enter with staggered motion.
* The surrounding layout adjusts smoothly.

When collapsing a branch:

* Descendant nodes fade out.
* Connecting lines retract.
* The layout reflows smoothly.

When selecting a person:

* The selected node receives a subtle highlight.
* Connected relationships become visually emphasized.
* The profile panel opens smoothly.

When adding new family members:

* New nodes appear in their proposed location.
* Pending nodes have a distinct visual treatment.
* Their connecting lines are animated.

When an addition is approved:

* The proposed node transitions into the normal approved visual state.

## Animation Timing

Prefer subtle durations around 200–500ms for normal UI interactions.

Use longer sequences only for cinematic landing-page moments.

Respect:

`prefers-reduced-motion`

When reduced motion is enabled:

* Disable decorative movement.
* Remove non-essential transitions.
* Keep the interface fully functional.

Performance and accessibility must take priority over decoration.

